Z||000025||sloth85GT||12-31-2001||05:45 AM||||What I wanna know is, is it possible to get one of those computer controlled keys that enables the starter and battery when you start the car and you can't start it without THAT key? Anyone know what I'm talking about? Is that available for a Fiero? I've heard they only cost about $200 or so to do a car.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">      <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>LT1 Coming Soon.....||||reg||1
Z||000026||avengador1||12-31-2001||09:15 AM||||A simple safeguard is to pull the fuel pump fuse and the coil wire. This will prevent them from hotwiring the car, It also would take time for them to figure this out and get the car running. Thieves don't have a lot of time to spend stealing a car so the more you do to stall them, the less likely they will be able to steal your car. A car alarm, the club, disconnecting the decklid release or a combination of all of these will help deter theft. The bottom line is if a thief wants your car he will do anything to get it. Its as simple a getting a flat bed to tow it away. I keep my car garaged when Im not using it and I don't take it everywhere I go. Let's face it our cars are very easy to steal as is any GM car. Check out the insurance statistics you will see this is true. I know it's hard to leave a car unattended for any period of time, but if you have a car that SCREAMS look at me, it's like ringing the dinner bell for thieves, so you have to be more carefull with it and take more security measures. The days of leaving our cars and houses unlocked are long gone. Sorry for my rant and I really am sorry for what happened to your car. Its a shame that we can't enjoy the fruit of our labors because some punks want our stuff and are too lazy to work for these themselves.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||fropuff||12-31-2001||10:34 AM||||I'm very sorry to hear that.  I think I am certainly going to put an alarm system in mine now.  What I would do is ask around; ask kids in your area if they know anything.  Try to find 'inside information' about chop shops or underground pawn shops.  I know for a fact that there is one here in my area, but no one really knows about it.  I could get any stereo equipment that I wanted for CHEAP through a kid at school.  I know it seems worthless to do it twice, but maybe you could buy your stuff back.  Either that or find out who did it and have them arrested.  I am very sorry to hear about your misfortune.  I know if someone stole my Fiero and dumped it into a f**king lake, I just don't know what I could or would do.  Hope everything turns out okay for you.||||reg||1
Z||000028||BAM-BAM||12-31-2001||10:54 AM||||  The saddest fact of all is that, nine times out of ten, it's some one that you know. I would look into some of the guys you hang with that aren't so close and may seem a little unsavory. It's obvious they knew what you had and where it was all located. They just waited till it was all done to get all that they could. Chances are, even if they catch them or have an idea who they are, the police won't waste the time to do much of anything. Our work trucks have been broken into 4 times in the past year. Each hit lost us over $50,000.00 worth of tools and equipment. Everything from Sawzalls, power drills, knock out sets, hand tools, digital protractors and levels, hydraulic benders and the list goes on. The police wouldn't even finger print the grease marks left by their hands. Said it's not worth the time or money to investigate that deeply. My  guess is that the doughnut shop was about to close and they didn't want to miss out on the free day olds (sarcasm).<BR>  Seriously, start looking into some of the creeps you know that might have an interest and knowledge of what you had. BTW was you car alarmed???<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>85GT 3.4L <BR>Eibachs and Poly's<BR>17" Konig Monsoons<BR>Kumho Ecstas<BR>Interior is all "Mike'd" up||||reg||9
Z||000029||Ken Wittlief||12-31-2001||11:39 AM||||ouch ouch ouch - that really sucks.<P> But you just gave me an idea - you know those keyless door locks they have on cars now? i wonder if you could buy the set, and insead of rigging it up as a door lock, wire it to the ECM or ignition so the car wont start unless you have the remote.<P> The same idea as the hidden secondary ignition switch, expect there is no switch to find.<P> it wouldnt stop someone from towing the car away, but would prevent the joyriders and smash and hotwire thiefs.||||reg||1
Z||000030||85 gt fiero||12-31-2001||12:50 PM||||that is (was) one nice ride i hope you have full coverage on it      i say we find the criminals and trash there cars <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
